Release archives published from this repository contain:

- couchlink.exe, built from the Rust sources in bridge/.
- couchlink-pico2w.uf2, built from the Pico 2 W firmware sources in pico-bridge/.
- couchlink-picow.uf2, built from the Pico W / Pico WH firmware sources in pico-bridge/.
- setup.ps1, the first-run PowerShell setup entrypoint.

The build uses Rust crates from crates.io and the Raspberry Pi Pico SDK. Those
components retain their own upstream licenses.

Portions of the PlayStation and Xbox One USB descriptor/report reference data
are adapted from GP2040-CE, Copyright (c) 2024 OpenStickCommunity
(gp2040-ce.info), licensed under the MIT License.

Firmware Joybus support uses libjoybus, Copyright (c) 2026 James Smith,
licensed under the MIT License.
